    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0172" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg162"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek
                        </hi><anchor n="95" xml:id="d128-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-10">November 10, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am terribly sorry to learn of Madame Chiang’s illness and sincerely hope that
                    she will be fully recovered in time for our conference.</p>
                <p>I have had a long talk with General Somervell and appreciate very much your
                    courtesies to him. He has given me your private message<anchor n="95a"
                        xml:id="d128-f2"/> as I have already indicated to you.</p>
                <p>I agree with you fully that we should meet together before I see Stalin. I want
                    so much to have some good talks with you so, naturally, I am eagerly looking
                    forward to seeing you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
